messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2025,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "AI systems match human experts at most cognitive tasks done on a computer.",
      "detail": "The timing is uncertain by several years either way. Deployment lags capability, but software, research and office work start to change quickly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "Humans return to the surface of the Moon.",
      "detail": "A US or Chinese crewed landing happens around the end of the decade, starting a slow build-up of lunar outposts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Global warming passes 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels as a long-term average.",
      "detail": "Emissions plateau and begin to fall, but too slowly to meet the Paris target. Heat extremes, fires and floods get noticeably worse."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "AI automation causes large-scale disruption of labor markets.",
      "detail": "Much white-collar work is automated and robotics begins doing the same for physical work. Governments try redistribution and new welfare models, with uneven success."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "AI systems do most scientific and engineering research.",
      "detail": "Discovery speeds up sharply in biology, materials and energy. Control and alignment of advanced AI becomes the central political and security issue."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "A major catastrophe involving advanced technology shocks the world.",
      "detail": "The most likely forms are an engineered pandemic, a serious AI-enabled attack or accident, or a great-power military crisis. I expect it to kill many people but not end civilization, and to lead to stricter global controls."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Superintelligent AI far exceeds humans in every domain.",
      "detail": "This is the most dangerous transition in the timeline. I put roughly a 10-25% chance on it leading to human extinction or permanent disempowerment this century; the rest of the timeline follows the more likely branch, where humans keep meaningful influence."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "The first humans land on Mars.",
      "detail": "The mission is made possible by cheap heavy launch and AI-run logistics. It is symbolically large but economically minor at first."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Material abundance becomes technically achievable for everyone.",
      "detail": "Cheap fusion and solar energy plus automated production make this possible. Distribution remains political and uneven, but extreme poverty largely ends."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Therapies that substantially slow or partly reverse aging become widely available.",
      "detail": "Healthy lifespans start to extend well beyond 100 years. This reshapes demographics, family life and politics."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "World population peaks below 10 billion.",
      "detail": "Low fertility pulls the biological population down afterward. Life extension and artificial wombs later complicate the trend."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global warming peaks at around 2-2.5°C.",
      "detail": "Emissions reach net zero and large-scale carbon removal begins. Major damage has already been done to coral reefs, ice sheets and many ecosystems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Digital minds are legally recognized as persons in major jurisdictions.",
      "detail": "These include AIs and possibly the first human brain emulations. They soon outnumber biological humans."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Permanent settlements on the Moon and Mars and in orbit hold tens of thousands of people.",
      "detail": "Machines do most of the industry in space. Biological humans remain a small part of off-world activity."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Most economic activity and energy use takes place off Earth.",
      "detail": "Automated industry mines asteroids and builds large solar collectors. Earth's industrial footprint shrinks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Atmospheric CO2 is brought back toward pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "Temperatures slowly fall, but seas keep rising for centuries because of ice-sheet inertia. Many coastal cities have been moved or walled off."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "The first serious interstellar probes are launched toward nearby stars.",
      "detail": "They are small, self-replicating machine probes travelling at a few percent of light speed or more."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Unmodified biological humans become a small minority of all persons.",
      "detail": "Most minds are digital, heavily enhanced or hybrid. Baseline humans persist by choice, with protection, mostly on Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Probes arrive at Alpha Centauri and other nearby systems and start building infrastructure.",
      "detail": "Local industry is built from asteroid material. Data, and later minds, are transmitted there from the Solar System."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Much of Earth is managed as a restored ecological and cultural preserve.",
      "detail": "A few billion or fewer biological humans live there. Some extinct species are revived and wild land expands."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "A partial Dyson swarm captures a significant fraction of the Sun's output.",
      "detail": "Civilization's energy use is many orders of magnitude above the 21st century's, and most of it goes to computation."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Self-sustaining civilizations exist in dozens of star systems within about 50 light-years.",
      "detail": "Light-speed delay makes unified government impossible. Cultures and values begin to diverge."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "A very large volcanic eruption (VEI 7 or greater) occurs on Earth.",
      "detail": "The date is arbitrary, but such an event is statistically likely within this span. For a civilization this advanced it is a manageable inconvenience."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "No language or institution from the 21st century survives in recognizable form.",
      "detail": "Nations, religions and languages of today exist only as archives and deliberately maintained traditions."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Descendant lineages have diverged into effectively separate species and kinds of mind.",
      "detail": "Biological, digital and collective intelligences differ enormously. The word \"humanity\" covers only part of what has descended from us."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "A major conflict or schism breaks out between diverging star systems or lineages.",
      "detail": "Over thousands of years and many independent societies, serious conflict is likely somewhere. Distance limits its spread, so it is unlikely to destroy the whole civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "The settled region reaches several hundred light-years from the Sun.",
      "detail": "Expansion proceeds at a sizeable fraction of light speed, led by self-replicating machines. Thousands of systems are occupied."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "The search for extraterrestrial intelligence has probably confirmed that our galactic neighborhood is empty.",
      "detail": "Surveys by enormous telescopes and probes most likely find at best simple life elsewhere. Detecting another technological civilization is possible but I think unlikely."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "The Solar System has been thoroughly re-engineered.",
      "detail": "Most asteroids and some moons and planets have been turned into habitats and computing structures. Earth is likely kept intact for its heritage value."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "The oldest continuous minds are thousands of years old.",
      "detail": "For most persons death is optional and rare, through backup and repair. Memory, identity and meaning across such spans become central concerns."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Earth's next ice age is deliberately prevented.",
      "detail": "Climate is actively controlled, overriding natural orbital cycles. Earth's environment is a managed artifact."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Descendants of humanity occupy a region perhaps a thousand or more light-years across.",
      "detail": "Millions of star systems hold a huge variety of minds. A small population of recognizably human beings probably still lives on Earth and elsewhere, if the transitions of the 21st and 22nd centuries went well."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "The decisive period is the next century or so, mainly the arrival of superintelligent AI together with engineered pandemics and great-power conflict. I put the chance of extinction or permanent disempowerment at roughly 15-30%, most of it before 2200, so I do not name an extinction year. If we get through, I expect our descendants, mostly digital or heavily modified, to spread among the stars and last far beyond the year 10000, with unmodified humans a small protected minority. Whether that counts as \"humanity\" still existing is partly a matter of definition, and everything after about 2100 is highly speculative."
}
